{"id":"056234534cd860b9","group":"58","path":"58/batch07/58-thm-inaccessible-properties.md","title":"Inaccessible Cardinal Properties","display":"thm-inaccessible-properties — Inaccessible Cardinal Properties","type":"theorem","metadata":{"type":"theorem","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-thm-inaccessible-properties","aliases":["58-thm-inaccessible-properties","Inaccessible Cardinal Properties","Strongly Inaccessible"],"display":"thm-inaccessible-properties — Inaccessible Cardinal Properties","depends_on":["[[../batch09/58-df-inaccessible.md]]","[[../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md]]","[[../batch03/58-df-assignment.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"theorem"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-thm-inaccessible-properties"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-thm-inaccessible-properties</span><span>Inaccessible Cardinal Properties</span><span>Strongly Inaccessible</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"thm-inaccessible-properties — Inaccessible Cardinal Properties"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"06ee5d7ff126e916\" href=\"?note=06ee5d7ff126e916\" title=\"../batch09/58-df-inaccessible.md\">../batch09/58-df-inaccessible.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"8b6a90316aad78a4\" href=\"?note=8b6a90316aad78a4\" title=\"../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md\">../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"64f35ba2e87964e0\" href=\"?note=64f35ba2e87964e0\" title=\"../batch03/58-df-assignment.md\">../batch03/58-df-assignment.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"65418b505fc53093\" href=\"?note=65418b505fc53093\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-formula.md\">../batch17/58-df-formula.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal L_\\in\">\\(\\mathcal L_\\in\\)</span> (language of set theory), <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\dot{\\in}\">\\(\\dot{\\in}\\)</span> (its binary membership symbol), and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{ZFC}\\subseteq\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_\\in)\">\\(\\mathrm{ZFC}\\subseteq\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathcal L_\\in)\\)</span> (set-coded ZFC axioms)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal V_\\kappa\">\\(\\mathcal V_\\kappa\\)</span> (canonical <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathcal L_\\in\">\\(\\mathcal L_\\in\\)</span>-structure with universe <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V_\\kappa\">\\(V_\\kappa\\)</span> and actual membership relation)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Univ}\">\\(\\mathrm{Univ}\\)</span> (structure-universe operator)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S\\)</span>, <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Assign}\">\\(\\mathrm{Assign}\\)</span>, and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"I^{\\mathcal M}_{\\mathrm{rel},2}\">\\(I^{\\mathcal M}_{\\mathrm{rel},2}\\)</span> (object-level semantic data)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{StronglyInaccessible}_S\">\\(\\mathrm{StronglyInaccessible}_S\\)</span> (strongly inaccessible-cardinal predicate)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> (cardinal)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}inaccessible\\text{-}properties}\\vdash \\mathrm{StronglyInaccessible}_S(\\kappa)\\to\\Bigl(\\exists\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat}\\;\\bigl[\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(\\mathcal V_\\kappa,\\mathcal L_\\in,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat})\\land\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal V_\\kappa)=V_\\kappa\\land I^{\\mathcal V_\\kappa}_{\\mathrm{rel},2}(\\dot{\\in})=\\{\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in V_\\kappa^2:x\\in y\\}\\land\\forall\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{ZFC}\\;\\forall s\\;(\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal V_\\kappa,s)\\to\\operatorname{Sat}(\\varphi,s))\\bigr]\\land\\forall\\lambda\\in\\kappa\\;(|V_\\lambda|&lt;\\kappa)\\land|V_\\kappa|=\\kappa\\Bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{thm\\text{-}inaccessible\\text{-}properties}\\vdash \\mathrm{StronglyInaccessible}_S(\\kappa)\\to\\Bigl(\\exists\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat}\\;\\bigl[\\mathrm{Satisfaction}_S(\\mathcal V_\\kappa,\\mathcal L_\\in,\\operatorname{Val},\\operatorname{Sat})\\land\\mathrm{Univ}(\\mathcal V_\\kappa)=V_\\kappa\\land I^{\\mathcal V_\\kappa}_{\\mathrm{rel},2}(\\dot{\\in})=\\{\\langle x,y\\rangle\\in V_\\kappa^2:x\\in y\\}\\land\\forall\\varphi\\in\\mathrm{ZFC}\\;\\forall s\\;(\\mathrm{Assign}(\\mathcal V_\\kappa,s)\\to\\operatorname{Sat}(\\varphi,s))\\bigr]\\land\\forall\\lambda\\in\\kappa\\;(|V_\\lambda|&lt;\\kappa)\\land|V_\\kappa|=\\kappa\\Bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Inaccessible: minimal large cardinal (if any).</li>\n<li>ZFC cannot prove existence.</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V_\\kappa\">\\(V_\\kappa\\)</span>: natural model when <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> inaccessible.</li>\n<li>Satisfaction of ZFC is witnessed by the registered recursion on the canonical set-coded membership structure; the theorem does not pass a raw metalinguistic <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\models\">\\(\\models\\)</span> relation into the object formula.</li>\n<li>If <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\kappa\">\\(\\kappa\\)</span> is inaccessible, then <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|V_\\lambda| &lt; \\kappa\">\\(|V_\\lambda| &lt; \\kappa\\)</span> for all <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\lambda &lt; \\kappa\">\\(\\lambda &lt; \\kappa\\)</span> and <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"|V_\\kappa| = \\kappa\">\\(|V_\\kappa| = \\kappa\\)</span>.</li>\n<li>The converse <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V_\\kappa\\models\\mathrm{ZFC}\\Rightarrow\\mathrm{Inaccessible}(\\kappa)\">\\(V_\\kappa\\models\\mathrm{ZFC}\\Rightarrow\\mathrm{Inaccessible}(\\kappa)\\)</span> is not asserted: ordinals with <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"V_\\kappa\\models\\mathrm{ZFC}\">\\(V_\\kappa\\models\\mathrm{ZFC}\\)</span> are called worldly and need not be inaccessible.</li>\n<li>Foundation for reflection arguments.</li>\n<li>Mahlo cardinals: limits of inaccessible cardinals.</li>\n<li>Consistency strength: above ZFC, below weakly compact.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch09/58-df-inaccessible.md","status":"resolved","id":"06ee5d7ff126e916","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch09/58-df-inaccessible.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md","status":"resolved","id":"8b6a90316aad78a4","anchor":"ref-2","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch18/58-df-satisfaction.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch03/58-df-assignment.md","status":"resolved","id":"64f35ba2e87964e0","anchor":"ref-3","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch03/58-df-assignment.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-formula.md","status":"resolved","id":"65418b505fc53093","anchor":"ref-4","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch17/58-df-formula.md]]","embed":false}],"math":[{"tex":"\\mathcal L_\\in","display":false},{"tex":"\\dot{\\in}","display":false},{"tex":"\\mathrm{ZFC}\\subseteq\\mathrm{Fml}_S(\\mathc